        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">For most people, the TriggerPoint GRID 1.0 is the foam roller to buy</strong>
            — firm, short, durable and inexpensive. Choose the TriggerPoint CORE if you are new to
            rolling or want a long roller for your spine, the RumbleRoller once you want more
            intensity, the GRID X only if the standard GRID feels too gentle, and a Vyper 3 or
            WaveRoller only if you already roll and want vibration as a comfort upgrade.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, roll slowly with moderate pressure for a minute or so per muscle, keep
